    "body":  "## Scope\n\nStacked on [#272](https://github.com/odango-chan/ca-skill-studio-demo/pull/272), which provides the canonical v2.1.0 Development Build request/digest builder.\n\nThis slice:\n- Pins the exact Compiler v2.1.0 source commit `b67fbb56c34d15b8d5a0903c8a7ca93d608f8f65`.\n- Downloads the official `skillc-v2.1.0-web-worker.tar.gz` release asset and verifies its checksum against the published `SHA256SUMS` before staging `skillc.wasm` and `wasm_exec.js`.\n- Adds `buildDevelopment` and `verifyDevelopment` to both browser and Node Worker protocols.\n- Re-verifies the resolver\u0027s existing Studio lock digest over original snapshot bytes before computing the separate Compiler v2.1.0 dependency digest; stale or tampered snapshots fail closed.\n- Exposes host integration methods to assemble a Development Build request from exact locked Interface Package snapshots and to verify its result.\n- Adds Node/WASM acceptance against the official Compiler fixture, including successful VerifyDevelopment, tampered artifact rejection and corrupted snapshot rejection.\n- Extends the real Theia Chromium smoke to run the same Development Build/Verify acceptance through the actual browser Worker.\n\nThe frozen v1alpha5 Build/Verify API remains tested as the Compiler\u0027s explicit frozen artifact-generator contract (generator identity v2.0.2); Studio product/runtime version is v2.1.0.\n\n## Not yet claimed\n\nThis does not yet switch Package Audit or AI Authoring\u0027s candidate gate to Development Build. It does not migrate project locks or supply trusted Owner/Capability bindings. Development result remains `NOT_ADMITTED`; no production admission or real-5GC qualification is claimed.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Exact source commit and published release bundle checksum.\n- Node Worker Development Build/Verify + negative tamper tests.\n- Browser Worker Development Build/Verify in Theia Chromium.\n- Existing frozen v1alpha5 artifact regression remains green.\n\n## Exact-head verification (2026-11-25)\n\nPASS on `7d6adebaca12f09d5ddc5e04f7457b8c15aa595e`: PR Verify, Native Windows standalone Authoring, IDE Host Spike, Theia Browser-Only Chromium, Theia Browser Host Chromium, Published Interface ZIP and Pages/default-root Chromium build (PR deployment skipped). The real browser Worker reports `VALIDATED / LINKED / BUILT / NOT_ADMITTED`, verifies the Development artifact, and rejects tampering. AI Editor Tab Apply/Undo acceptance is synthetic Mock Gateway evidence only.\n\nPR remains OPEN / Draft / unmerged and stacked on the exact current #272 HEAD. Package Audit and AI Authoring\u0027s authoritative Development Build candidate gate remain open in #269.\n\n## Current branch freshness (2026-11-25)\n\nThe exact-head CI above passed on `7d6adebaca12f09d5ddc5e04f7457b8c15aa595e`. Since then, the #272 base branch has advanced by 9 commits; this Worker branch is **9 commits behind its current base** and must be reapplied/rebased after #272 is refreshed onto current `main`. Historical PASS is not a current merge gate. Rerun PR Verify, Native Windows, IDE Host, Theia Browser-Only, Theia Browser Host, Published Interface ZIP and Pages Chromium on the rebased exact head. PR remains OPEN / Draft / unmerged.\n\nThe Worker proves Compiler v2.1.0 API/Worker parity on the official synthetic fixture; it does not yet make the current MAS Example buildable because its `mas` and `ca-context` Contract roots are currently locked as non-Interface-Package kinds. See [Issue #269](https://github.com/odango-chan/ca-skill-studio-demo/issues/269).",
